  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The race for Missouri's 2nd Congressional District pits 13-term Republican incumbent Rep. Ann Wagner against multiple primary challengers from both parties, with the general election winner to be determined after the August 4, 2026 primary. The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee placed this district on its target list for 2026, the first time it has targeted Wagner since 2020, citing shifting suburban voting patterns. The Democratic primary features three candidates — veteran and podcast host Fred Wellman, teacher Joan VonDras, and physician Tim Bilash — while Wagner faces Republican primary challenges from Elizabeth Sparks-Holmes, Peter Pfeifer, Ryan Sheridan, and Brandon Wilkinson. The district covers St. Louis's western and southern suburbs plus Franklin County, and a 2025 redistricting map signed by Gov. Mike Kehoe has made the seat somewhat more Republican-leaning, though the map faces ongoing legal challenges.",
